From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dora SSR <dora@ippclub.org>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Include cmath for ImageData NaN handling

Android NDK 21 does not expose std::isnan through ImageData's transitive
headers. Include the standard header directly, preserving the existing NaN
clamp behavior on all platforms.

Upstream: LOVE 11.5, commit 6eb8d546736d5915a8b5af30b2cf33456dfdcb1a
Compatibility: build-only fix; runtime behavior is unchanged.
---
 src/modules/image/ImageData.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/modules/image/ImageData.cpp b/src/modules/image/ImageData.cpp
index 79c3fe7..b02f2dd 100644
--- a/src/modules/image/ImageData.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/image/ImageData.cpp
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #include "ImageData.h"
 
 #include <algorithm> // min/max
+#include <cmath> // isnan
 
 using love::thread::Lock;
 
